  <title>Manufacturing</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>General</gui><gui>Manufacturing</gui></guiseq> opens the
  <gui>Manufacturing Overview</gui>, which lists the projects being built. A
  project builds a number of one manufactured product from the parts in its
  <link xref="assembled_products">assembled product</link> list. Posting the
  project takes the parts out of stock and puts the finished products
  in.</p>

  <section id="new">
  <title>Starting a project</title>
  <steps>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Product</gui> and the <gui>Version</gui> of its
    parts list, and how many to <gui>Manufacture</gui>. The
    <gui>Manufacturing name / description</gui> is filled in; change it if you
    like.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Stock destination</gui>, the location the
    finished products go to.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check <gui>Available in Time Clock</gui> to let employees punch
    in on the project.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Create project</gui>. The parts needed are listed
    below.</p></item>
  </steps>
  <p>To change a project later, select it in the overview and click
  <gui>Edit</gui>. Change its fields and click <gui>Update project</gui>, or
  <gui>Save</gui> to keep the changes and close the window. <gui>Batch
  notes</gui> are kept with the project.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="parts">
  <title>Parts needed</title>
  <p>Each part shows the <gui>Needed qty</gui>, how many are <gui>On
  hand</gui> at its <gui>Source</gui> location, and in <gui>All
  locations</gui>. Only stock at the source counts: stock elsewhere has to be
  moved there first. <gui>Order qty</gui> is the shortfall.</p>
  <list>
    <item><p>Click a part's <gui>Part</gui> to use a substitute, its
    <gui>Source</gui> to take it from another location, or its
    <gui>Vendor</gui> to order it from someone else. Type the vendor's
    <gui>Order #</gui> if it is not filled in.</p></item>
    <item><p>Select parts and click <gui>Add to PO</gui> to add their order
    quantities to each vendor's open <link xref="purchase_order"/>. If the
    part is already on that order you are asked whether to raise its
    quantity. The <gui>Status</gui> then reads Added; right click and choose
    <gui>View PO</gui> to see the order.</p></item>
    <item><p>Scan a barcode or type an order number into <gui>Add part by
    barcode or order #</gui>, or click <gui>Add part</gui>, to add a part the
    list does not have. Right click a part to delete it, or to open its
    <gui>Product hub</gui>.</p></item>
  </list>
  <p>If the parts list was changed after the project was created, <gui>Sync
  from BOM</gui> adds and removes parts to match it, keeping the
  substitutions and vendors already chosen. <gui>Reload from BOM</gui>, in the
  window menu, throws the whole list away and starts again from the parts
  list, after asking.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="serial_numbers">
  <title>Serial numbers</title>
  <p>For a product sold by serial number, select the project in the overview
  and click <gui>Serial numbers</gui>.</p>
  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the label <gui>Printer</gui> and <gui>Template</gui> under
    <gui>Print options for this window</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Check the first number under <gui>Generate serial number(s)</gui>;
    the last one is shown after <gui>to</gui>. Set how many labels to
    <gui>Print</gui> of each.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Generate</gui>. A serial number is made for each
    unit still without one, and its labels print.</p></item>
  </steps>
  <p>To print a label again, choose the <gui>Serial number</gui> and click
  <gui>Reprint</gui>, or right click it in the list and choose
  <gui>Print</gui>. Only one person can work on a project's serial numbers at
  a time.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="post">
  <title>Posting a project</title>
  <p>When the products are built, select the project in the overview and
  click <gui>Post project</gui>. The parts come out of stock at their source
  locations, the finished products go into stock, and the project leaves the
  time clock and the list.</p>
  <p>Posting is refused while a serial numbered product is missing serial
  numbers. If the parts take stock below zero, you are told which and asked
  whether to post anyway.</p>
  </section>

</page>
